<title>GERMANY: Henkel no comment on Loctite bid refusal.</title>
<headline>Henkel no comment on Loctite bid refusal.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Henkel KGaA said on Monday it had no comment on Monday on a call by its takeover target, U.S. Loctite Corp, to reject its bid terms.</p>
<p>A Henkel spokesman said no statement was planned after Loctite directors rejected its bid for control as inadequate and said they were &quot;determined to seek to sell the company at a price that fully reflects its value.&quot;</p>
<p>Henkel has bid $57.75 a share for the 65 percent of Loctite it does not already own. The offer was below the $59-3/4 price at which Loctite was trading late morning in New York.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
